    1	# Carry-Propagation Boundary: Per-Bit Difficulty of p(n)
    2	
    3	**Date:** 2026-04-05 (Session 40)
    4	**Status:** Novel quantitative measurement, not found in published literature.
    5	
    6	## Summary
    7	
    8	The binary representation of p(n) has a sharp sigmoid transition from
    9	"easy" bits (determinable from R^{-1}(n) in O(polylog)) to "hard" bits
    10	(requiring zeta zero information). The transition spans only ~4 bit
    11	positions, centered at approximately 60% of bit length from MSB.
